{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1697 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "73864ac26d96052f00bd8409bbf27bce579258f09ffc9250a4d9e1d790818a00" :edb/db-before-t 1696 :edb/db-after-t 1697 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535009 50 #inst "2026-10-08T14:16:20.115Z" 13194139535009 true] [17592186064081 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326437 13194139535009 true] [17592186064081 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326458 13194139535009 true] [17592186064081 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326465 13194139535009 true] [17592186064081 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326479 13194139535009 true] [17592186064082 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326444 13194139535009 true] [17592186064082 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326451 13194139535009 true] [17592186064082 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326472 13194139535009 true] [17592186326437 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326438 13194139535009 true] [17592186326437 1089 "q-20982" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326437 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535009 true] [17592186326437 1100 "For the function $f(x)=-{x}^{4}+2{x}^{2},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $x=-1$ is a relative minimum of $f(x)$\n- $x=0$ is a relative minimum of $f(x)$\n- ${f}^{″}(1)>0$\n- $x=1$ is a relative maximum of $f(x)$" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326437 1113 #uuid "c8611a54-1200-5e47-8def-2e7361f092cb" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326437 1145 "We need to identify the critical points. Then, we then need to classify them using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=-{x}^{4}+2{x}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-4{x}^{3}+4x,\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4{x}^{3}+4x & =0 \\\\ -4x({x}^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ -4x(x-1)(x+1) & =0 \\\\ x & =-1,0,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=-1,0,1.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at the critical points. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=-12{x}^{2}+4,\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at each critical point, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(-1) & =-8<0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(0) & =4>0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(1) & =-8<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that:\n\n- Statement I is false. The second derivative is negative at $x=-1,$ so this is a relative maximum of $f(x).$\n\n- Statement II is true. The second derivative is positive at $x=0,$ so this is a relative minimum of $f(x).$\n\n- Statement III is false while statement IV is true. The second derivative is negative at $x=1,$ so this is a relative maximum of $f(x).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and IV only.\"" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326438 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326439 13194139535009 true] [17592186326438 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326440 13194139535009 true] [17592186326438 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326441 13194139535009 true] [17592186326438 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326442 13194139535009 true] [17592186326438 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326443 13194139535009 true] [17592186326438 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535009 true] [17592186326438 1041 "selection" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326438 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326441 13194139535009 true] [17592186326438 1110 #uuid "ce1120dc-53cd-505d-8efa-af7d97ec23d9" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326439 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326439 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326439 1111 #uuid "b0cf53f9-5781-5380-809b-ea89525ff95b" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326440 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326440 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326440 1111 #uuid "ece12859-35e4-5b1e-90a7-d39b6b4f2f63" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326441 1034 "II and IV only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326441 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326441 1111 #uuid "0c31177e-a508-56c1-a6c7-3bb21a5ba7c6" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326442 1034 "I only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326442 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326442 1111 #uuid "90aad3df-60f3-546c-b14f-df2ff03f3599" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326443 1034 "III and IV only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326443 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326443 1111 #uuid "c1d42aa4-0b17-5fff-8211-7f9419b8a1bf" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326444 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326445 13194139535009 true] [17592186326444 1089 "q-20983" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326444 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535009 true] [17592186326444 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)=2{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}+24x.$ Given that ${f}^{′}(2)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(2)=0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=2$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=2$" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326444 1113 #uuid "36b293da-b761-54d5-a1fa-c581da4bd74e" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326444 1145 "We're given that $x=2$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)=2{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}+24x,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=6{x}^{2}-24x+24.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=12x-24.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(2) & =12\\cdot 2-24=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is zero, we conclude that the test is inconclusive, we need to use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's  find other stationary points. These points are the solution of the equation ${f}^{′}(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-24x+24 & =0 \\\\ 6(x-2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the only stationary point is $x=2.$\n\nLet's choose auxiliary points from each side of the stationary point and evaluate the first derivative at them. We take the auxiliary points $x=1,3$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & =6(1)^{2}-24(1)+24=6>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(3) & =6(3)^{2}-24(3)+24=6>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince the first derivative does not change the sign at $x=2$, we conclude that $f(x)$ has no relative extrema at this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326445 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326446 13194139535009 true] [17592186326445 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326447 13194139535009 true] [17592186326445 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326448 13194139535009 true] [17592186326445 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326449 13194139535009 true] [17592186326445 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326450 13194139535009 true] [17592186326445 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535009 true] [17592186326445 1041 "selection" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326445 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326446 13194139535009 true] [17592186326445 1110 #uuid "a0bc78c7-6707-55ea-88a7-9bfae578b2d4" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326446 1034 "I only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326446 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326446 1111 #uuid "632cc29c-24ac-5199-ace3-c4ebe736bf79" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326447 1034 "III only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326447 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326447 1111 #uuid "2cae57a4-1c98-55dc-883b-9c6bf2a596f1" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326448 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326448 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326448 1111 #uuid "77755ba8-def3-5c1b-a91b-8a76933cff1c" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326449 1034 "None of the statements are true." 13194139535009 true] [17592186326449 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326449 1111 #uuid "a3d02997-ea04-59fe-ad3a-8d5c0678d29f" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326450 1034 "II only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326450 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326450 1111 #uuid "03657456-da74-5805-a5f6-a75f5a4c927f" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326451 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326452 13194139535009 true] [17592186326451 1089 "q-21498" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326451 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535009 true] [17592186326451 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)=2{x}^{2}+8x-5.$ Given that ${f}^{′}(-2)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(-2)>0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=-2$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=-2$" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326451 1113 #uuid "c31f870a-ef31-544a-816e-4bdd0cd35f53" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326451 1145 "We're given that $x=-2$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)=2{x}^{2}+8x-5,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=4x+8.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=4.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(-2) & =4>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is positive, we conclude that $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326452 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326453 13194139535009 true] [17592186326452 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326452 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326455 13194139535009 true] [17592186326452 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326456 13194139535009 true] [17592186326452 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326457 13194139535009 true] [17592186326452 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535009 true] [17592186326452 1041 "selection" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326452 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326456 13194139535009 true] [17592186326452 1110 #uuid "514ccdd2-9312-5872-b8f5-637896fd2874" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326453 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326453 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326453 1111 #uuid "069fe1be-1247-51f4-b98f-c05c1176dfc6" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326454 1034 "I only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326454 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326454 1111 #uuid "e13aaaa5-b4a4-5770-86a4-99455dc8f95a" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326455 1034 "III only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326455 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326455 1111 #uuid "14af8cff-bbe3-52eb-8d33-1703c82b9961" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326456 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326456 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326456 1111 #uuid "88db4ab1-5c45-5d7b-8a83-173003bdea66" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326457 1034 "II only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326457 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326457 1111 #uuid "12c5e1b3-f4dc-546d-b852-dedaba5440a4" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326458 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326459 13194139535009 true] [17592186326458 1089 "q-22015" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326458 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535009 true] [17592186326458 1100 "For the function $f(x)=3{x}^{5}-10{x}^{3}+9,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $x=\\sqrt{2}$ is a critical point of $f(x)$\n- ${f}^{″}(\\sqrt{2})<0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=\\sqrt{2}$" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326458 1113 #uuid "cb8bdfe9-f8e3-5c06-a75c-ba841bd3ac3d" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326458 1145 "We need to identify whether $x=\\sqrt{2}$ is a critical point. If it is, we then need to classify it using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=3{x}^{5}-10{x}^{3}+9,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=15{x}^{4}-30{x}^{2},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15{x}^{4}-30{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 15{x}^{2}({x}^{2}-2) & =0 \\\\ 15{x}^{2}(x+\\sqrt{2})(x-\\sqrt{2}) & =0 \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{2},0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=\\pm \\sqrt{2},0.$ We're interested in the critical point $x=\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at this critical point. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=60{x}^{3}-60x,\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=\\sqrt{2}$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(\\sqrt{2})=60(\\sqrt{2})^{3}-60\\sqrt{2}=60\\sqrt{2}>0.\n$$\n\nThe second derivative is positive at $x=\\sqrt{2},$ so this critical point is a relative *minimum*. \n\nTherefore, comparing our results with the given statements, we conclude that:\n\n- $x=\\sqrt{2}$ is a critical point of $f(x)\\,✓$\n\n- ${f}^{″}(\\sqrt{2})>0\\,\\times $\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative *minimum* at $x=\\sqrt{2}\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326459 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326460 13194139535009 true] [17592186326459 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326461 13194139535009 true] [17592186326459 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326462 13194139535009 true] [17592186326459 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326463 13194139535009 true] [17592186326459 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326464 13194139535009 true] [17592186326459 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535009 true] [17592186326459 1041 "selection" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326459 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326461 13194139535009 true] [17592186326459 1110 #uuid "6bb9326b-7e50-581e-966d-94d00343cf40" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326460 1034 "None of the statements are true" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326460 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326460 1111 #uuid "38850f22-cb0f-594a-9fcf-4d893c83ad09" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326461 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326461 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326461 1111 #uuid "35775a19-d1da-5cf9-baf2-c789afab5545" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326462 1034 "I only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326462 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326462 1111 #uuid "4c012390-24b4-56e4-8ac5-c2389ac83fbb" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326463 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326463 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326463 1111 #uuid "45726da9-9813-5a76-a2e9-c190e044365e" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326464 1034 "II only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326464 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326464 1111 #uuid "f852aed0-4599-55c4-ac83-28f4e3f3eb7a" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326465 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326466 13194139535009 true] [17592186326465 1089 "q-22137" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326465 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535009 true] [17592186326465 1100 "For the function $f(x)=2{x}^{5}-5{x}^{4}+10,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $x=2$ is a critical point of $f(x)$\n- ${f}^{″}(2)>0$\n- $x=2$ is a relative  minimum of $f(x)$" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326465 1113 #uuid "c0c817fa-2470-5a07-8886-20bbcad704ac" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326465 1145 "We need to identify whether $x=2$ is a critical point. If it is, we then need to classify it using the second derivative test\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=2{x}^{5}-5{x}^{4}+10,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=10{x}^{4}-20{x}^{3},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10{x}^{4}-20{x}^{3} & =0 \\\\ 10{x}^{3}(x-2) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=0,2.$ We're interested in the critical point $x=2.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at this critical point. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=40{x}^{3}-60{x}^{2},\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at each critical point, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(2)=40(2)^{3}-60(2)^{2}=80>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second derivative is positive at $x=2,$ so this critical point is a relative *minimum*.\n\nTherefore, comparing our results with the given statements, we conclude that:\n\n- $x=2$ is a critical point of $f(x)\\,✓$\n\n- ${f}^{″}(2)>0\\,✓$\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative *minimum* at $x=2\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"." 13194139535009 true] [17592186326466 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326467 13194139535009 true] [17592186326466 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326468 13194139535009 true] [17592186326466 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326469 13194139535009 true] [17592186326466 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326470 13194139535009 true] [17592186326466 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326471 13194139535009 true] [17592186326466 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535009 true] [17592186326466 1041 "selection" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326466 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326467 13194139535009 true] [17592186326466 1110 #uuid "daff2a2d-e402-55ac-a5c8-43f7e8087b87" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326467 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326467 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326467 1111 #uuid "84fdbc77-cd92-505d-b931-17809e867237" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326468 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326468 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326468 1111 #uuid "0f036490-643f-53a2-9ab8-2321e479121f" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326469 1034 "I only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326469 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326469 1111 #uuid "2bb86a07-fbd0-5a3d-8243-3f02107457b8" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326470 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326470 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326470 1111 #uuid "8fc6e4b7-5958-59a0-9e45-67e4ea83c5e3" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326471 1034 "II only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326471 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326471 1111 #uuid "f7b8f4d0-e993-5c53-8145-05c606ecdaa2" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326472 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326473 13194139535009 true] [17592186326472 1089 "q-22147" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326472 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535009 true] [17592186326472 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)={x}^{4}-8{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-32x+12.$ Given that ${f}^{′}(2)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(2)=0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=2$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=2$" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326472 1113 #uuid "36ca3da0-e647-5cc4-ad2d-0df0027c82be" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326472 1145 "We're given that $x=2$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)={x}^{4}-8{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-32x+12,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =4{x}^{3}-24{x}^{2}+48x-32 \\\\  & =4({x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+12x-8) \\\\  & =4(x-2)^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=12(x-2)^{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(2) & =12(2-2)^{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is zero, we conclude that the test is inconclusive, we need to use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's  find the stationary points. These points are the solution of the equation ${f}^{′}(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x-2)^{3} & =0 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the only stationary point is $x=2.$\n\nLet's choose auxiliary points from each side of the stationary point and evaluate the first derivative at them. We take the auxiliary points $x=1,3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & =4(1-2)^{3}=-4<0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(3) & =4(3-2)^{3}=4>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince the first derivative changes the sign at $2$  from minus to plus, we conclude that $x=2$  is a relative minimum.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326473 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326474 13194139535009 true] [17592186326473 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326475 13194139535009 true] [17592186326473 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326476 13194139535009 true] [17592186326473 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326477 13194139535009 true] [17592186326473 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326478 13194139535009 true] [17592186326473 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535009 true] [17592186326473 1041 "selection" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326473 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326477 13194139535009 true] [17592186326473 1110 #uuid "721c2b23-147b-58af-84a8-fa07e80b6c1e" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326474 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326474 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326474 1111 #uuid "42df6b4a-2af2-5931-9584-c8c1042d3096" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326475 1034 "I only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326475 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326475 1111 #uuid "5b9c3aa1-adf6-5c2b-84fc-ec0969fd87aa" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326476 1034 "III only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326476 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326476 1111 #uuid "bc64d6ae-2bba-56ba-8adf-0139851ef502" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326477 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326477 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326477 1111 #uuid "99690c50-80df-57d7-8614-b52a4658358c" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326478 1034 "II only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326478 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326478 1111 #uuid "c2eea50f-7235-5c19-a94d-43cda0270c66" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326479 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326480 13194139535009 true] [17592186326479 1089 "q-22495" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326479 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535009 true] [17592186326479 1100 "For the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is a critical point of $f(x)$\n- ${f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})<0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326479 1113 #uuid "1ac0fc85-8ffe-585d-b5ca-13b862035cec" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326479 1145 "We need to identify whether $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is a critical point. If it is, we then need to classify it using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x) & =0 \\\\ 2x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi , \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}.$ We're interested in the critical point $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at this critical point. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})=-2<0.\n$$\n\nThe second derivative is negative at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ so this critical point is a relative *maximum*. \n\nTherefore, comparing our results with the given statements, we conclude that:\n\n- $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is a critical point of $f(x)\\,✓$\n\n- ${f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})<0\\,✓$\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative *maximum* at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326480 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326481 13194139535009 true] [17592186326480 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326482 13194139535009 true] [17592186326480 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326483 13194139535009 true] [17592186326480 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326484 13194139535009 true] [17592186326480 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326485 13194139535009 true] [17592186326480 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535009 true] [17592186326480 1041 "selection" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326480 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326484 13194139535009 true] [17592186326480 1110 #uuid "7436ab63-239e-5781-aa5a-3b04197a8987" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326481 1034 "None of the statements are true" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326481 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535009 true] [17592186326481 1111 #uuid "50b9fae5-34e2-5792-a8c9-495014932d96" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326482 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535009 true] [17592186326482 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 131941395350